// pfodWeb NOTE: excludes GPIO4/14/27/32/33 (dedicated TFT display CS/
// DC/RST/backlight + microSD CS - not even declared in this boards own
// pins_arduino.h, only in the M5Stack librarys Config.h) and GPIO5/18/
// 19/23 (shared TFT+SD SPI bus) - confirmed via M5Stack Arduino library
// source + official docs.
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO39 tagged "button" - confirmed docs.m5stack.com/en/core/basic
// (Custom buttons x3, pinmap Button A=G39) + M5Stack Arduino library
// Config.h (BUTTON_A_PIN 39) + Button.cpp read() using digitalRead().
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO38 tagged "button" - confirmed docs.m5stack.com/en/core/basic
// (pinmap Button B=G38) + M5Stack Arduino library Config.h (BUTTON_B_PIN 38)
// + Button.cpp read() using digitalRead() (plain GPIO, not capacitive touch).
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO37 tagged "button" - confirmed docs.m5stack.com/en/core/basic
// (pinmap Button C=G37) + M5Stack Arduino library Config.h (BUTTON_C_PIN 37)
// + Button.cpp read() using digitalRead() (plain GPIO, not capacitive touch).
// pfodWeb NOTE: no onboard user LED found for this board (original M5Stack
// Core Basic/Gray/Go) - M5Stack library Config.h only defines TFT_LED_PIN
// (GPIO32), which is the TFT backlight, not a user-controllable indicator
// LED, and GPIO32 is already excluded above (dedicated display pin).
{
  "boardName": "ESP32",
  "displayName": "ESP32 Dev Module",
  "family": "esp32",
  "pwm": {
    "min": 0,
    "max": 255,
    "method": "analogWrite"
